      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T13:40:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Native git doesn\u0027t lock either — git refs migrate documents it as a known limitation (\"no way to block concurrent writes during an ongoing migration … users are expected to block writes on a higher level\").\n\nThe JGit swap is non-atomic, and the SSH convert-ref-storage command has shipped that way since 2021. Rather than add a guard, I documented the limitation on both the REST endpoint and the SSH command here.\n\nA read-only guard spanning both paths could still be a follow-up if we want one.",
      "parentUuid": "d33f0925_b7e288db",
      "revId": "e24b0c710dcc95f0e2aaabc953149072663d3017",
